            "review_title": "Review at Crystal Jade Palace Le Loi",
            "review_text": "Vy H.\nWashington DC, District of Columbia7159 contributions\n0\nDinner in Ho Chi Minh, Vietnam\nMar 2024 • Friends\nThe restaurant is quite fancy, clean and spacious, but overall the food was just okay. Came here randomly Friday evening for dinner with no reservations—we got seated upstairs in a big booth for party of 6, but the restaurant was fairly empty.\n\nFood was underwhelming. First off, they don’t offer ANY dishes from the dim sum menu (lunch), not even as an a la carte order. Sautéed Soft Shell Crab with Salted Egg Yolk was decent, Szechuan Hot & Sour Prawn Soup was not well flavored enough, Deep-fried Prawn with Mayo was overly drenched with mayo, Sautéed Beef Cubes in Black Pepper was over cooked and Wok-Fried Hor Fun with Beef was okay. Most disturbing dish was the Roasted Peking Duck—they bring out the whole duck for you to see, then proceeds to de-skin it and makes the rolls for you—not sure why, but over 5 staff members were hovering over the duck to do this. Then they serve us the rolls with NO duck meat inside!!! This is not Peking duck rolls, this is just the duck skin, a piece of cucumber and onion with hoisin sauce. Terrible. They offer to cook your duck meat as a separate dish (with rice or noodles, etc) for extra charge. So confused as to why there was no duck inside my Peking DUCK roll.\n\nOverall, food is pricey here and not worth it. Personally, I don’t think this place is worthy of a Michelin star.\nRead more\nWritten March 25, 2024",
